      "message": "These tests had bad expectations. In std140, a 2x2 matrix is still aligned on 16 bytes, so the required alignment should be 16.\n\nIn the old UniformManager code, the helper function `sksltype_to_alignment_mask` did not account for std140\u0027s conservative array alignment. For actual offset calculations, the layout was checked before calling `sksltype_to_alignment_mask` inside `get_ubo_aligned_offset` to switch to querying alignment for `kFloat4`. However, the required alignment was updated in `writeInternal` by just calling `sksltype_to_alignment_mask`.",
